# Text files are LF in the repository AND in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) gives every file CRLF endings, and a
# wheel built there ships CRLF while one built on Linux ships LF -- the same release, byte
# different, depending on who ran `uv build`. Nothing breaks at run time; it just makes the
# artifact impossible to reproduce or compare. `eol=lf` rather than bare `text=auto` because
# only the explicit form settles the WORKING TREE, which is what the build reads.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, whatever the content sniffer thinks.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.whl binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.parquet binary
*.npy binary
*.safetensors binary
